G5023.b:
⟪οὗτος⟫, αὕτη, τοῦτο, gen., τούτου, ταύτης, τούτου,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨זֶה⁩, ⁨זֹאת⁩;] demonstr. pron. (related to ἐκεῖνος as hic to ille), ⟪this⟫;
⟪1.⟫ as subst., ⟪this one⟫, ⟪he⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ absol.: ⟦Matthew 3:17|Mt 3:17⟧, ⟦Mark 9:7|Mk 9:7⟧, ⟦Luke 7:44|Lk 7:44⟧, ⟦Luke 7:45|45⟧, ⟦John 1:15|Jo 1:15⟧, ⟦Acts 2:15|Ac 2:15⟧, al.; expressing contempt (cl.), ⟦Matthew 13:55|Mt 13:55⟧, ⟦Matthew 13:56|56⟧, ⟦Mark 6:2|Mk 6:2⟧, ⟦Mark 6:3|3⟧, ⟦John 6:42|Jo 6:42⟧, al.; εἰς τοῦτο, ⟦Mark 1:38|Mk 1:38⟧, ⟦Romans 14:9|Ro 14:9⟧; μετὰ τοῦτο (ταῦτα; V. Westc. on ⟦John 5:1|Jo 5:1⟧), ⟦John 2:12|Jo 2:12⟧ ⟦John 11:7|11:7⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ epanaleptic (referring to what precedes): ⟦Matthew 5:19|Mt 5:19⟧, ⟦Mark 3:35|Mk 3:35⟧, ⟦Luke 9:48|Lk 9:48⟧, ⟦John 6:46|Jo 6:46⟧, ⟦Romans 7:10|Ro 7:10⟧, al.;
	⟪(c)⟫ proleptic (referring to what follows): seq. ἵνα (Bl., § 69, 6), ⟦Luke 1:43|Lk 1:43⟧, ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧ (and freq.) ⟦John 15:8|15:8⟧, ⟦Romans 14:9|Ro 14:9⟧, al.; seq. ὅτι, ⟦Luke 10:11|Lk 10:11⟧, ⟦John 9:30|Jo 9:30⟧, ⟦Acts 24:14|Ac 24:14⟧, ⟦Romans 2:3|Ro 2:3⟧, al.; ὅπως, ⟦Romans 9:17|Ro 9:17⟧; ἐάν, ⟦John 13:35|Jo 13:35⟧;
	⟪(d)⟫ special idioms: τοῦτο μὲν . . . τ. δέ (cl), ⟪partly . . . partly⟫, ⟦Hebrews 10:33|He 10:33⟧; καὶ τοῦτο (τοῦτον, ταῦτα), ⟪and that⟫ (⟪him⟫) ⟪too⟫, ⟦Romans 13:11|Ro 13:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:2|I Co 2:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:12|He 11:12⟧; τοῦτ’ ἐστιν, ⟪that is to say⟫, ⟦Matthew 27:46|Mt 27:46⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As adj., c. subst.;
	⟪(a)⟫ c. art.
		⟪(α)⟫ before the art.: ⟦Matthew 12:32|Mt 12:32⟧, ⟦Mark 9:29|Mk 9:29⟧, ⟦Luke 7:44|Lk 7:44⟧, ⟦John 4:15|Jo 4:15⟧, ⟦Romans 11:24|Ro 11:24⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:9|Re 19:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(β)⟫ after the noun: ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧, ⟦Mark 12:16|Mk 12:16⟧, ⟦Luke 11:31|Lk 11:31⟧, ⟦John 4:13|Jo 4:13⟧, ⟦Acts 6:13|Ac 6:13⟧, ⟦Romans 15:28|Ro 15:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:20|I Co 1:20⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:24|Re 2:24⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ c. subst. anarth. (with predicative force; Bl., § 49, 4): ⟦Luke 1:36|Lk 1:36⟧ ⟦Luke 2:2|2:2⟧ ⟦Luke 24:21|24:21⟧, ⟦John 2:11|Jo 2:11⟧ ⟦John 4:54|4:54⟧ ⟦John 21:14|21:14⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 13:1|II Co 13:1⟧.

G5007.b:
⟪τάλαντον⟫, -ου, τό
[in LXX for ⁨כִּכָּר⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a balance⟫ (Hom.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪that which is weighed, a talent⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ a talent in weight (in Horn. always of gold);
⟪(b)⟫ a sum of money, whether gold or silver, equivalent to a talent in weight (v. DB, iii, 418 ff.): ⟦Matthew 18:24|Mt 18:24⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:15|25:15⟧ff.†

G5043.b:
⟪τέκνον⟫, -ου, τό
(< τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨בֵּן⁩, also for ⁨יֶלֶד⁩, etc. ;] that which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish bairn), ⟪a child⟫ of either sex: ⟦Mark 13:12|Mk 13:12⟧, ⟦Luke 1:7|Lk 1:7⟧, ⟦Acts 7:5|Ac 7:5⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 7:11|Mt 7:11⟧, ⟦Mark 7:27|Mk 7:27⟧, ⟦Luke 1:17|Lk 1:17⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:1|Eph 6:1⟧, al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, ⟦Romans 9:8|Ro 9:8⟧; τ. τῆς σαρκός, ⟦Romans 9:8|ib.⟧; in a wider sense (as Heb. ⁨בָּנִים⁩), of posterity, ⟦Matthew 2:18|Mt 2:18⟧, ⟦Luke 3:8|Lk 3:8⟧, al.; specif., of a male child, ⟦Matthew 21:28|Mt 21:28⟧, ⟦Acts 21:21|Ac 21:21⟧, a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, ⟦Matthew 9:2|Mt 9:2⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:28|21:28⟧, ⟦Mark 2:5|Mk 2:5⟧, ⟦Luke 2:48|Lk 2:48⟧; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; v. Bl., §37, 5), ⟦Galatians 4:19|Ga 4:19⟧ (τεκνία, WH, txt.), ⟦2 Timothy 2:1|II Ti 2:1⟧. Metaph.,
⟪(a)⟫ of disciples (apart from direct address, v. supr.): ⟦Philemon 1:10|Phm 10⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 1:2|I Ti 1:2⟧, ⟦Titus 1:4|Tit 1:4⟧, ⟦3 John 1:4|III Jo 4⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ with reference to the Fatherhood of God (v.s. πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. ⟦Isaiah 30:1|Is 30:1⟧, Wi 16:21): ⟦Romans 8:16|Ro 8:16⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:1|Eph 5:1⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:15|Phl 2:15⟧; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, Epp. Jo., 94, 120), ⟦John 1:12|Jo 1:12⟧, ⟦1 John 3:1|I Jo 3:1⟧ al.;
⟪(c)⟫ of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars: ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧, ⟦Luke 3:8|Lk 3:8⟧, ⟦John 8:39|Jo 8:39⟧, ⟦Romans 9:7|Ro 9:7⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:6|I Pe 3:6⟧; τ. διαβόλου, ⟦1 John 3:10|I Jo 3:10⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ as in Heb. (LXX, ⟦Joel 2:23|Jl 2:23⟧, ⟦Psalms 149:2|Ps 149:2⟧, I Mac 1:38), of the inhabitants of a city: ⟦Matthew 23:37|Mt 23:37⟧, ⟦Luke 13:34|Lk 13:34⟧ ⟦Luke 19:44|19:44⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:25|Ga 4:25⟧;
⟪(e)⟫ with an adjectival gen., freq. rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (v. Deiss., BS, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, ⟦Ephesians 5:8|Eph 5:8⟧; τ. ὑπακοῆς, ⟦1 Peter 1:14|I Pe 1:14⟧; κατάρας, ⟦2 Peter 2:14|II Pe 2:14⟧; ὀργῆς, ⟦Ephesians 2:3|Eph 2:3⟧.
SYN.: v.s. παῖς.
